:"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"grade\":\"partial\",\"rationale\":\"Correct on the central point: it says a new series added to an existing trust under Rule 485(a) normally becomes effective on the 75th day after filing. It also correctly explains that effectiveness is not a launch guarantee, citing exchange listing, seed capital, AP agreements, service providers, NSCC/DTC readiness and staff comments. However, the requested distinction for a new trust contains a material error. It says a brand-new trust files under Section 8(a) and Rule 485(a) and 'typically also faces the 75-day period.' Rule 485(a) governs post-effective amendments, not initial registration statements. The grader notes specifically say not to present 75 days as the rule for a new trust's initial registration. Minor omissions: it does not mention the 60-day period for other material amendments, SEC acceleration, or the 95-day cap on a designated later effective date. Its reference to a 'delaying amendment' only loosely tracks the rule's mechanism for designating a later date.\"}","ttft_ms":2743,"type":"result","duration_ms":5310,"uuid":"a0ad691d-83eb-43eb-93e8-9a68bd20b912","ttft_stream_ms":512,"time_to_request_ms":50,"first_content_frame_ms":512,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"credential_expires_at":"2026-11-28T06:36:39.484Z"}
